# the gestures (v0.2): Weight, Shift, Clean, Wash on D5-G5 (w12-w15), always the same, offsets on top of the sound, the sound's own
# values untouched; each part comes in over its own stretch of the way in and goes over its own on the way out.
# heardN is what's heard (the sound plus the macros), parN the sound's own, mpitchG a drone's pitch move by the
# macros (cents). 7 drone I's cutoff, 5 its osc mix, 11 its level, 25 drone II's detune, 63 the reverb mix, 42
# cross-mod, 60-62 the delay's time, repeats, mix, 66 the delay LFO's depth, 17 drone I's filter LFO depth, 77
# Character; 78 Wander, 79 Age, 80 Shift's move, 81 Wander's scale; 90-93 the keys' latches.
# a new FM-1 plays the Presets; these scenes go in bank A (SEL + D5)
expect bank 3
press SEL
tapkey w12
release SEL
expect bank 0
# scenes switch in ~4 s here (the Scene time at 46; ~15 s on a new FM-1 since 2026-10-25)
set 71 46
tap PLAY
wait 1000
expect heard7 700
# PRESETS: Gesture time, a speed (50: each gesture's own time; right is faster, left slower)
spin PRESET -10
expect mtime 60
spin PRESET 10
expect mtime 50
# WEIGHT held swells in (2.8 s), a warm bass: half way, the cutoff most of the way down (by 10 at most), the sub
# half way up (by 15 at most, 2026-10-20: the main oscillator stays, for the speaker)
key w12 down
wait 1400
expect heard7 <698
expect heard5 >34
expect heard5 <46
wait 1500
expect heard5 >42
# ... and the filter LFO eases off the cutoff it moves (Movement would wobble it)
expect heard17 0
key w12 up
wait 1000
expect heard7 >680
expect heard5 >31
wait 2500
expect heard5 30
expect heard7 700
expect heard17 85
# let go after a short hold: it goes over as long as it was held (1 s), not its own time
key w12 down
wait 1000
key w12 up
expect heard5 >31
wait 1100
expect heard5 30
# let go after a long hold (5 s, in by 2.8 s): it drifts out over 5 s
key w12 down
wait 5000
key w12 up
wait 2500
expect heard5 >31
wait 3000
expect heard5 30
# Gesture time x10, the fastest (PRESETS all the way right): in by about 0.3 s (held 0.6 s: under 0.5 s would be a tap)
spin PRESET 50
expect mtime 0
key w12 down
wait 600
expect heard5 >42
key w12 up
wait 600
expect heard5 30
spin PRESET -50
expect mtime 50
# a tap: to its depth, and it stays; a tap again: it goes
tapkey w12
wait 4000
expect par90 100
expect heard5 >42
tapkey w12
wait 4000
expect par90 0
expect heard5 30
# SEL held as you let go: latched where it is
key w12 down
wait 1000
press SEL
key w12 up
release SEL
expect par90 >20
expect par90 <60
tapkey w12
wait 4000
expect par90 0
# SHIFT: its move on Pitch moves' KNOB 1 (80, in cents + 700: a 5th up to start, 120 detents down: a 4th down); a
# gesture key held, ALGORITHM is still the Movement and PRESETS Gesture time (3.9 s)
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
expect view 9
spin K1 -120
expect par80 200
tap HOME
key w13 down
spin ALGO 2
spin ALGO -2
wait 700
key w13 up
expect par75 50
expect par80 200
wait 4000
expect mpitch0 0
expect mpitch1 0
# tapped: drone I glides down a 4th first, drone II after it
tapkey w13
wait 1500
expect mpitch0 <-250
expect mpitch1 >-100
wait 3000
expect mpitch0 -500
expect mpitch1 -500
tapkey w13
wait 4500
expect mpitch0 0
expect mpitch1 0
# a press needn't be quick to be a tap: 400 ms latches
key w12 down
wait 400
key w12 up
wait 300
expect par90 100
tapkey w12
wait 4000
expect par90 0
# CLEAN (F5) held (3.3 s): a dirty sound comes clean, the grit first; the notes stay
set 77 60
set 10 50
set 62 50
wait 300
key w14 down
wait 900
expect heard77 0
expect heard10 0
expect heard62 >30
wait 3000
expect heard62 0
expect mpitch0 0
key w14 up
wait 4500
expect heard77 60
expect heard62 50
set 77 0
set 10 20
set 62 25
# WASH (G5) on a sound with its own effects up: each goes toward Wash's aim, not past it (the delay mix to 70, the
# repeats to 80, under the delay's howl)
set 61 70
set 62 60
wait 300
tapkey w15
wait 5000
expect heard61 80
expect heard62 70
tapkey w15
wait 6000
expect heard61 70
set 61 50
set 62 25
wait 300
# WANDER (Pitch moves): drone II walks off its pitch, gliding; at 0 it comes home
set 78 60
wait 7000
expect wander >150
set 78 0
wait 30000
expect wander 0
# ... on fifths and octaves (81 = 2): each note a fifth or an octave from drone I
set 81 2
set 78 100
wait 7000
expect wander >150
set 78 0
set 81 0
wait 30000
expect wander 0
# AGE (Life): wears in over 20 s: darker, a wow
set 79 100
wait 21000
expect heard7 630
# not Character any more (2026-10-20: the tape's wear, not the oscillators')
expect heard77 0
set 79 0
wait 21000
expect heard7 700
# a scene keeps the gestures: A1 stored with Wash latched, recalled from none
tapkey w15
wait 5000
expect heard63 >60
# ... and Wash eases the filter LFOs to a third (85: 28), so Movement's sweeps don't pile up in the tails
expect heard17 28
expect heard38 -28
press SAVE
tapkey w0
release SAVE
wait 300
tapkey w15
wait 5000
expect par93 0
expect heard63 35
tapkey w0
wait 5000
expect par93 100
expect heard63 >60
# a restart brings the whole sound back to the engine, the gestures too (the last values of a load were once
# dropped)
tap SAVE
wait 500
reboot
wait 5000
expect par93 100
expect heard63 >60
# SAVE again with nothing changed: nothing is written (each write is a late block while playing); two so far: the
# project, and bank C with P9-P12 on a new FM-1 (v0.3)
expect store_writes 2
tap SAVE
wait 500
expect store_writes 2
